  "detail": "this is an ExecutionReceipt v2, and the issuer's deployed rule makes a v1-v4 verdict historical and snapshot-relative: it requires the exact preserved registry snapshot bytes, their full SHA-256 and their byte length with every such verdict, and says to fail closed when they are absent. No --registry was supplied, so there is no snapshot for a verdict to be relative to and none is stated. --allow-unregistered-signer does NOT waive this: that flag speaks about the signer, this is about the scope of the whole result. Supply the registry bytes preserved with this receipt — never current.json and never the current registry, which the rule forbids substituting",
